course: dictionary
lesson: 3031
title: Earache: a pain and a complaint
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Earache» means a pain inside your ear. Read the context to see which meaning fits: «Earache can be an infection, so you tell an adult.» Here the sentence is about your body, so the pain is in your ear.
explain: Some words have a second, informal meaning. If someone says you are giving them earache, they are not talking about ears at all. They mean you are nagging them or talking at them too much.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is the sentence about a body or about a person's behaviour? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: «Earache» means a pain inside your ear.
fact: «Earache» is a noun, so you can say «an earache» or «earaches».
fact: In British English, people often say «have earache», but in American English people say «have an earache».
fact: Informally, «giving someone earache» means nagging them or talking at them too much.
fact: «Earache can be an infection, so you tell an adult.»
exercise: «Earache can be an infection, so you tell an adult.» What does earache mean? | A bad smell from a bin | *A pain inside your ear | Food that tastes sour | A loud noise in the kitchen
exercise: Mum says, «Stop giving me earache about your homework!» What does giving someone earache mean here? | Singing very softly to them | Making someone's ear hurt with cold water | *Nagging someone or talking at them too much | Buying someone a present
exercise: Ella says, «I have earache, so I need to see the doctor.» Which phrase is the usual British way to say it? | I have a ear ache | I got earache from the sun | *I have earache | I have an earache
test: «The little boy cried all night with a bad earache.» What is a bad earache? | A bad smell from the ear | A long hug from a friend | *A strong pain inside the ear | A game played on a bus
test: Dad says, «Please stop giving me earache about the car.» What does he mean? | He is pleased with the car | *He wants you to stop nagging him | He has a pain in his ear | He wants the car fixed by a doctor
exam: Earache can be an infection. What should you do if you have earache? | Shout loudly until it stops | Put your fingers in your ears | Ignore it and go out to play | *Tell an adult
